    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of the changes I made.\n\n## Changes\n\n**1. `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier` string-enum property (`GOLD`/`SILVER`/`BRONZE`) with `membershipLevel`, a `readOnly` integer constrained to `minimum: 1`, `maximum: 3`, documenting the creation-time formula. Since `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec at build time, this is what removes the old field and adds the new one to the response.\n\n**2. `src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Swapped the `@Mapping` target from `membershipTier` to `membershipLevel`, and replaced `toMembershipTier(...)` (which returned the enum) with `toMembershipLevel(...)`:\n- start at 1\n- +1 when an email is present\n- +1 when `namesakeCount == 0`\n- capped at 3 via `Math.min(level, 3)`\n\n**3. `src/main/java/.../function/owner/AssignHouseholdSize.java`** \u2014 Removed the now-stale javadoc sentence about the mapper deriving the `GOLD` tier from `householdSize` (household size no longer factors into the level; I left the field/assignment itself intact as it's still persisted).\n\n## Notes\n- The spec's clause about \"anything that recorded the tier (such as the create audit line)\" was conditional \u2014 I verified `AuditOwnerCreated` logs only `id`, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`; it never recorded the tier, so no audit change was needed. (Confirmed at runtime: `AUDIT - Owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-LEV-0001 registrationDate=...`.)\n- The new acceptance test `coreNumericLevel` (email + unique name \u2192 level 3, capped) passes, and the full suite is green: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
